    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1014">

                <pb facs="1067" n="1057" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1057"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.AJ Treaties/6–349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-03T12:00:00+08:00">June 3,
                            1949—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 11:31 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1183. Received Tihwa’s 139 to Department. Assume Chinese Government expects
                    register with United Nations terms any and all agreements concluded over
                    Sinkiang.</p>
                <p>Sent OffEmb Canton 486; repeated Department 1183, Tihwa 39.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
